Dear AI Engineering Hiring Team at Icertis,

Vera Agents shipping as semi-autonomous contracting agents inside customer guardrails moves the hard problem of applied AI from generation to provable control. A contract agent that advances an obligation must show which clause authorized the step and which source it read, a boundary I have engineered against directly.

At *LexoLegal*, I built the *Munshi* WhatsApp legal assistant in *Python* with *Pydantic AI* and *FastAPI*, orchestrating *Model Context Protocol (MCP)* clients across Google Drive and Calendar at *sub-2s latency*. Tenant identity lives in agent dependencies rather than tool parameters, so a crafted prompt cannot widen its own reach, and every inbound *WhatsApp* webhook is signature checked before dispatch. The layer underneath is 38 asynchronous *REST APIs* in *FastAPI* and *SQLAlchemy* over 12 *PostgreSQL* tables, covered by *1,024 Pytest tests*.

Grounding claims need measurement. In *ncert-rag-evals* I benchmarked 8 retrieval strategies over 17 textbooks and proved that Reciprocal Rank Fusion of *BM25* and *ChromaDB* embeddings reached *86.9% Recall\@5 in 8.9ms on CPU*, a *99.8% latency cut* validated by paired McNemar tests (*p = 0.0021*) across 92 *Pytest* tests. In *vectorless-rag* I measured a *100% retrieval hit rate* against *93%* for vector search at *0.85* citation precision. On the interface side, *doubtless* streams *SSE* tokens into a *React 19* and *TypeScript* workspace with *AbortSignal* cancellation.

Icertis runs a Microsoft-centric platform, and my production work is Python, React, and PostgreSQL, so I would pick up the .NET and Azure side quickly while contributing where my evidence is strongest. I am enrolled in a B.Tech in Computer Science through 2027 and can join a 6-month internship in Pune full time, on site five days a week, with in-person interviews.

